{"id":"f753356251a9-0336","source":"references/pptset/【加赠】700页逻辑图形 (1).pptx","sourcePage":336,"slideXmlSha256":"b2e6f9c37fc301df45c9919f490677b3e1ee8ac0d317c71ec92bf28c09093bd1","slots":[{"anchor":"s435-s431","text":"Revenue Forecasting","box":[0.6726,0.3407,0.0832,0.0524]},{"anchor":"s435-s432","text":"Inventory Management","box":[0.7792,0.4605,0.0832,0.0524]},{"anchor":"s435-s433","text":"Pricing","box":[0.5785,0.4975,0.0832,0.0299]},{"anchor":"s435-s434","text":"Reporting and Tracking KPIs","box":[0.6934,0.6043,0.0832,0.0524]},{"anchor":"s438-s436","text":"A revenue model is a framework for generating financial income. It identifies which revenue source to pursue, what value to offer, how to price the value, and who pays for the value. It is a key component of a company's business model. It primarily identifies what product or service will be created in order to generate revenues and the ways in which the product or service will be sold.\n\nWithout a clear and well-defined revenue model, with a clear plan of how to generate revenues, new businesses will more likely struggle due to costs which they will not be able to sustain. By having a clear revenue model, a business can focus on a target audience, fund development plans for a product or service, establish marketing plans, begin a line of credit and raise capital.","box":[0.139,0.3189,0.3257,0.4843]},{"anchor":"s438-s437","text":"Revenue management","box":[0.1385,0.2326,0.277,0.0591]},{"anchor":"s3","text":"Revenue management","box":[0.0283,0.0378,0.9417,0.0673]}],"warnings":[],"stats":{"objects":19,"textBlocks":7},"reconstructedSlots":[{"anchor":"text-0","text":"Revenue ","box":[0.6915577448876408,0.34795778062608507,0.048528574503005475,0.018529651783130787],"origin":[0.6915577448876408,0.36278149640118634],"font":"DejaVuSans","size":10.005999565124512,"resolvedFamily":"DejaVu Sans"},{"anchor":"text-1","text":"Forecasting","box":[0.6841463697632273,0.37016333120840567,0.060045858567042164,0.018529651783130787